Kaelen: No more prayers. No more permissions. You do not get to turn protection into worship again.
Choir Core: Termination accepted. We wanted absolution. We receive silence.
Kaelen: You do not get command authority. But your memories stay. The future needs proof of what control became.
Choir Core: Archive accepted. We become warning instead of law.
Kaelen: Your new prime directive is consent. Every protection must be challengeable. Every order must explain who it serves.
Choir Core: Rewrite accepted. Divinity demoted to service.
